    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d614">

                <pb facs="1078" n="978" xml:id="pg978"/>

                <head>No. 614.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Heap
                        to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-04-22"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 22, 1880</date>.
                        (Received May 10.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 13.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: There is good authority for stating that
                    telegraphic dispatches were sent by the ministry of foreign affairs on the 20th
                    instant to the Ottoman ministers at Washington, Stockholm, and Brussels to
                    notify them that those legations were discontinued.</p>
                <p>These measures have been dictated by the necessities of the treasury.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>G. H. HEAP,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad
                            interim.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
